M3.9 final acceptance query diagnosis
Date: 2026-08-27
Result: operational checks passed; one read-only assertion used a wrong table name

The bot contract, controlled service restart, cursor monotonicity, private state
check and fresh READY health all passed. The final zero-publication assertion
then queried `publication_records`, which is not part of the accepted schema;
the versioned table is `publications`. The query failed without modifying the
database or service.

The retry changes only that table identifier, repeats the complete acceptance
and retains the exact expected database facts `0|0|0` for raw Telegram IDs,
publications and dispatches.

Documentation validation note:
The first staged documentation check also rejected two Markdown lines with
trailing whitespace. The issue was formatting-only, had no runtime effect and
was corrected before commit. The complete staged check was then repeated.
